        {"at": [2.54, 5.08], "drill": 1.7, "src": "kicad-mx", "what": "a peg of a 5-pin switch"},
        {"at": [-6.35, 2.54], "drill": 3.05, "src": "kicad-mx", "srcPad": "2", "drillSrc": "kailh", "what": "the socket's hole for the switch's pin A, 3.05 +-0.05"},
        {"at": [0, 0], "drill": 3.05, "src": "kicad-mx", "srcPad": "1", "drillSrc": "kailh", "what": "the socket's hole for the switch's pin B, 3.05 +-0.05"}
      ],
      "holeNote": "kicad-mx drills the two pins 1.5 mm for a soldered switch; under a socket they are the socket's holes, sized by kailh. marbastlib drills those 3.0 and its pegs 1.75, keebio its pegs 1.7. Kailh's 2016 and 2021 revisions print the hole as 3.00 (research/keypad-pcb-footprints.md section 5)."
